    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "1d16e1bf-c6ec-30fc-9d49-19145ea27d10",
                "word": "tutelary",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "afbf55b9-6a37-4e6f-b19f-d96ca5269ffc",
                        "entry_id": "1d16e1bf-c6ec-30fc-9d49-19145ea27d10",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more tutelary"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "29dfd210-db0a-4ebd-ab57-1661c22c31e2",
                        "entry_id": "1d16e1bf-c6ec-30fc-9d49-19145ea27d10",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most tutelary"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3ff76e4a-67d2-3250-ab3c-91c883aa5f01",
                        "entry_id": "1d16e1bf-c6ec-30fc-9d49-19145ea27d10",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Relating to guardianship or protection."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b12c3117-e10a-4298-98e3-9e0766884280",
                                "sense_id": "3ff76e4a-67d2-3250-ab3c-91c883aa5f01",
                                "text": "When a minor is involved, tutelary powers frequently accompany powers of attorney."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ad8d44bc-6b83-44ab-a62f-13794769b25d",
                                "sense_id": "3ff76e4a-67d2-3250-ab3c-91c883aa5f01",
                                "text": "[I]n the firſt of Henry the ſixth, the Company of Armorers in London were incorporated by the name of the fraternite of Saint George: which queſtionleſſe reflected on him, though not as Patron ſpecially of this Realme of England, yet as the tutelarie Saint of militarie men. Elſe to what purpose ſhould the Armorers, whoſe trade is onely deſtinate to the uſe of Souldiers, be made a Corporation by his name, and under his protection."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4e7771f0-dc32-4bde-96b6-97078db9d1a7",
                                "sense_id": "3ff76e4a-67d2-3250-ab3c-91c883aa5f01",
                                "text": "The iſland [of Lemnos] was conſecrated to Vulcan, whom the inhabitants worſhiped as their tutelary god. They were believed to have been the firſt blackſmiths, which gave the poets the occaſion to feign, that Vulcan, when he was thrown down from heaven, fell in the iſland of Lemnos, where he built his forge."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ab070ced-6b5c-4dd2-89cb-aaa0722a5a60",
                                "sense_id": "3ff76e4a-67d2-3250-ab3c-91c883aa5f01",
                                "text": "In our Athenian constitution, if we are weakly governed or capriciously, which hardly can happen, the mischief is transitory and reparable; one year closes it; and the people, both for its satisfaction and its admonition, sees that no corruption, no transgression, in its magistrates, is unregarded or unchastized. This, of all advantages, is the greatest, the most corroborative of power, the most tutelary of morals."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "088f2968-ffe6-4778-a5a2-3b39b890e386",
                                "sense_id": "3ff76e4a-67d2-3250-ab3c-91c883aa5f01",
                                "text": "Our contemporaries are constantly excited by two conflicting passions: they want to be led, and they wish to be free. As they cannot destroy either the one or the other of these contrary propensities, they strive to satisfy them both at once. They devise a sole, tutelary, and all-powerful form of government, but elected by the people. They combine the principle of centralization and that of popular sovereignty; this gives them a respite: they console themselves for being in tutelage by the reflection that they have chosen their own guardians."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fffe26a3-bea4-44f5-9094-2bee56ef77b2",
                                "sense_id": "3ff76e4a-67d2-3250-ab3c-91c883aa5f01",
                                "text": "[T]he goat-herd lived / As calmly, underneath the pleasant brows / Of cool Lucretilis, where the pipe was heard / Of Pan, Invisible God, thrilling the rocks / With tutelary music, from all harm / The fold protecting."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7c74534e-2b90-4185-a2c1-d93f0ccef874",
                                "sense_id": "3ff76e4a-67d2-3250-ab3c-91c883aa5f01",
                                "text": "The tutelary genius of mankind / Ripens by slow degrees the final State, / That in the soul shall its foundations find / And only in victorious love grow great; / Patient the heart must be, humble the mind, / That doth the greater births of time await!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d9a96c52-0149-46a5-8600-0bc2d731c2eb",
                                "sense_id": "3ff76e4a-67d2-3250-ab3c-91c883aa5f01",
                                "text": "In Antwerp, for instance, as late as the sixteenth century Priapus was the tutelary god of the city."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5b10a3d3-48f7-4ede-901d-de08ac4a6360",
                                "sense_id": "3ff76e4a-67d2-3250-ab3c-91c883aa5f01",
                                "text": "There are two kinds of ancestral spirits. Some represent founders of the individual family, while others represent founders of the community, such as priests and kings. The spirits of founders of communities are called \"territorial\" or \"tutelary spirits\" in the literature for the region. Tutelary spirits cut across family lines because they belong to the community and are evoked on its behalf (generally only for rainmaking). They are associated with public proscriptions, and their propitiation is controlled by chiefs, kings, and priests."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7fbeeb00-5932-4fe5-810c-b910f04adadd",
                                "sense_id": "3ff76e4a-67d2-3250-ab3c-91c883aa5f01",
                                "text": "The tutelary state is a protective and regulatory state. As De Tocqueville argued, the independent persons of the democratic age, when they find themselves vulnerable, look outward for assistance. They can't receive it from their equals, who are disinterested, so they look for it from the state. Yet the idea of equality forbids, absolutely, this state providing social guarantees in a politically despotic manner. That would re-introduce personal dependency in a new guise. Clientelism, patrimonialism, patronage would be returned. So a new kind of state is required. This is the administrative or tutelary state. It instantiates a new kind of rule—the rule of knowledge—and as we shall see in a minute—also a new kind of power or sovereignty—viz. Democratic Power or Democratic Sovereignty."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cd911ae4-26e4-329a-af08-4c4a5204228e",
                        "entry_id": "1d16e1bf-c6ec-30fc-9d49-19145ea27d10",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of or pertaining to a guardian."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1bcf16d4-af4d-4d91-9f47-5df03e1517bf",
                                "sense_id": "cd911ae4-26e4-329a-af08-4c4a5204228e",
                                "text": "My uncle is always happy to discharge his tutelary responsibilities towards me."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0bdccc25-ad45-4768-a7c8-0d64c2b0528e",
                                "sense_id": "cd911ae4-26e4-329a-af08-4c4a5204228e",
                                "text": "[T]he Duke withdrew him to Roan, and from thence to the King of France, to craue his aid, putting him in minde of, the faithfull ſeruice his father had done him: how he was his homager, vnder his tutelarie charge, and had no other ſanctuary of ſuccour to flie vnto, in this caſe of his mutinous and turbulent nobilitie; the effect whereof was of dangerous conſequence to that Crowne."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e44513ee-b197-43fe-ab36-c3fbcd3776f7",
                                "sense_id": "cd911ae4-26e4-329a-af08-4c4a5204228e",
                                "text": "At St. Regis' Amory stayed three days and took his exams with a scoffing confidence, then doubling back to New York to pay his tutelary visit. […] [Monsignor Darcy] and Amory took to each other at first sight—the jovial, impressive prelate who could dazzle an embassy ball, and the green-eyed, intent youth, in his first long trousers, accepted in their own minds a relation of father and son within a half-hour's conversation."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "42f9f63a-3504-4f63-a9a0-240e6f5be830",
                                "sense_id": "cd911ae4-26e4-329a-af08-4c4a5204228e",
                                "text": "As we were deep in the Shan country, there were no more pagodas, but shrines had been erected on the town's outskirts to the tutelary spirits, and some of them were hung with votive offerings of puppet-horses."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5d292975-b9ca-39b4-a4b6-85fd0d3ce736",
                        "entry_id": "1d16e1bf-c6ec-30fc-9d49-19145ea27d10",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having the qualities of a tutor."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f549f902-334c-414f-8460-15b551cd6fd8",
                                "sense_id": "5d292975-b9ca-39b4-a4b6-85fd0d3ce736",
                                "text": "She loved him so passionately, and he was so godlike in her eyes; and being, though untrained, instinctively refined, her nature cried for his tutelary guidance. And thus, though Tess kept repeating to herself, 'I can never be his wife,' the words were vain."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1972eab6-3391-47af-a455-3f69692e6abe",
                        "source_entry_id": "1d16e1bf-c6ec-30fc-9d49-19145ea27d10",
                        "source_sense_description": "having guardianship or protection of",
                        "target_lang_word": "tutélaire",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tutélaire",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ef1c4201-3848-3c93-bf79-9d0d617d8eef",
                                        "entry_id": "8de6f7da-f6d7-363b-a77b-c2a421c07800",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui tient sous sa garde, sous sa protection."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8fb1b935-f2a2-43a1-b3f1-4c89c399b8cd",
                                                "sense_id": "ef1c4201-3848-3c93-bf79-9d0d617d8eef",
                                                "text": "Dans le style allégorique, on disoit que Jupiter où Minerve avoit prêté l’ægide à tel héros, à tel prince, pour indiquer la protection que ces divinités tutélaires lui accordoient."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eb63d737-55bd-4fcd-b8d9-6f6b4569dcf5",
                                                "sense_id": "ef1c4201-3848-3c93-bf79-9d0d617d8eef",
                                                "text": "[…] et à Dieu ne plaise qu’elle ait réclamé de nous sans l’avoir obtenue la protection de nos lois tutélaires."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "55bdc7be-d9d9-4631-b3e8-77092c64e3a4",
                                                "sense_id": "ef1c4201-3848-3c93-bf79-9d0d617d8eef",
                                                "text": "Enfin, c’est celui qui veut remplacer la loi tutélaire de la majorité par l'arbitraire tyrannique du petit nombre, faire le peuple esclave du parti & écraser la démocratie tout entière sous une despotique kakistocratie."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1998184a-a0f9-4147-8a47-ff97151d04d1",
                                                "sense_id": "ef1c4201-3848-3c93-bf79-9d0d617d8eef",
                                                "text": "Elles insinuaient aussi une sorte de caresse tutélaire, de fraîcheur balsamique, d’aide lustrale."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fa03594c-c20f-4316-8b93-ac8960f27215",
                                                "sense_id": "ef1c4201-3848-3c93-bf79-9d0d617d8eef",
                                                "text": "À croire que quelque ange tutélaire avait entendu sa pensée, la porte s'ouvrit et une dame avenante lui demanda : — Que prenez-vous pour votre petit déjeuner, monsieur Triggs ?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e57fd06-a210-4ee8-ba58-beaa9bb9cb87",
                                                "sense_id": "ef1c4201-3848-3c93-bf79-9d0d617d8eef",
                                                "text": "Durant son séjour dans la capitale, il refusa d’accomplir des sacrifices à son ancêtre tutélaire et à ses ancêtres agnatiques."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f1af9837-31be-3bbf-b08e-8774bc8aa84c",
                                        "entry_id": "8de6f7da-f6d7-363b-a77b-c2a421c07800",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Relatif aux tutelles."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0bd0b68a-5696-483c-9555-7784c4bb72e1",
                                                "sense_id": "f1af9837-31be-3bbf-b08e-8774bc8aa84c",
                                                "text": "Tant la doctrine que la jurisprudence estiment pourtant aujourd’hui que la refonte du droit tutélaire doit tabler sur un plus grand professionnalisme dans la protection des mineurs et des adultes"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
